ufs: free the ufs_buffer_head in ubh_bforget()

ubh_bread() allocates a struct ufs_buffer_head that ubh_brelse() frees but
ubh_bforget() does not, so free_full_branch(), its only caller, leaks one
per indirect block it frees. The same fix was proposed in 2018 ("ufs: Fix
memory leak in the unlink path", Luis Henriques) but is not in mainline.
---
--- a/fs/ufs/util.c	2026-10-20 16:53:32.835970204 +0000
+++ b/fs/ufs/util.c	2026-10-20 16:53:32.846490364 +0000
@@ -119,6 +119,7 @@
 		return;
 	for ( i = 0; i < ubh->count; i++ ) if ( ubh->bh[i] ) 
 		bforget (ubh->bh[i]);
+	kfree(ubh);
 }
  
 int ubh_buffer_dirty (struct ufs_buffer_head * ubh)
